  Status: author draft; independent mathematical and Lean correspondence
  review pending. Source revision: <verbatim|3456e5e75cf8d4cd558955a5c7638fba2d68f464>.

  <section|Scope><label|scope>

  The manuscript is <verbatim|manuscript/existence/centered-geyser-scale-estimates.tex>.
  It spells out the real-variable estimates used by the selected public
  Geyser producer and the finite-prefix construction turning each
  transition's eventual estimates into one monotone delay sequence. It does
  not prove the selected nonlinear menu response, the selected purchase, or
  the upstream construction of its fixed schedule/profile data.

  <section|Source correspondence><label|source-correspondence>

  <block|<tformat|<twith|table-width|1par>|<twith|table-hmode|exact>|<cwith|1|-1|1|-1|cell-hyphen|t>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-bborder|1ln>|<cwith|1|1|1|-1|cell-valign|bottom>|<table|<row|<cell|<strong|Manuscript
  assertion>>|<cell|<strong|Pinned declaration and
  file>>|<cell|<strong|Inspection notes>>>|<row|<cell|Entrance scale and
  shifted beta>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.Pressure.radiusB>,
  <verbatim|YM.Pressure.betaF>; <verbatim|Lean/YM/Pressure/Seeds.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|radiusB(x)=ceil((log
  x)^2)> and <verbatim|betaF G x L=x+G.slopeConstant*log L.val>. The constant
  shift is fixed for a fixed period. <verbatim|radiusB> tends to infinity by
  <verbatim|Work.E01.radiusB_tendsto>.>>|<row|<cell|Reciprocal polynomial
  reserve>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.winter>, <verbatim|fog>,
  <verbatim|sap>, <verbatim|stub>; <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Bandage.tableCost>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Tender.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Kettle.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|winter>,
  <verbatim|fog>, <verbatim|sap>, and <verbatim|stub> are in
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof>; the selected title cost, <verbatim|tableCost>, is
  in <verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Bandage> in
  <verbatim|Kettle.lean>. The displayed power is <verbatim|degree(frame
  d)+4>; <verbatim|stub(x)=Hat(x)/4>; title cost is twice
  <verbatim|exp(supportExponent)> times the finite title bound. Stage column
  counts and orbit costs are finite fixed quantities for the selected
  schedule.>>|<row|<cell|Polynomial growth under the subexponential mint
  allowance>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.polestar>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Tender.lean>>|<cell|Its proof first bounds
  <verbatim|(x+b)^q> by <verbatim|x^(q+1)> for fixed <verbatim|b,q>; the
  logarithmic threshold then gives <verbatim|(q+1)log x\<leq\>(log
  x)^2/128\<leq\>radiusB(x)/128>. We gave this exact argument in ordinary
  notation. <verbatim|mintK(B)=exp(B/128)> is
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Menu.mintK> in <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Paddle.lean>.>>|<row|<cell|Contact/stain
  reserve>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.dew>;
  <verbatim|YM.Extra.Multi.site_affords>, <verbatim|hat_affords>,
  <verbatim|vacuum_affords>; <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Tender.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Extra/MULTISOURCE_BOUNDS/Delays.lean>>|<cell|The source
  obtains <verbatim|Hat\<leq\>1/4>, <verbatim|smallK\<leq\>Hat^6>, and
  <verbatim|(1+p siteFactor(B))(2B+1)^4 Hat\<leq\>1>. Since
  <verbatim|Doors.stain=smallK^2>, this implies stain\<leqslant\>Hat, and the
  contact exponent is bounded by <verbatim|(1+p siteFactor(B))Hat>. The
  factor <verbatim|(2B+1)^4\<geq\>2> yields exponent\<leqslant\>1/2 and
  <verbatim|e^(1/2)-1\<less\>1>. The three underlying reserve eventual
  estimates have their own proofs in <verbatim|Delays.lean>, including the
  quartic site-factor growth bound.>>|<row|<cell|Five reciprocal radial
  estimates and stencil fit>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.rind>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Tender.lean>>|<cell|For fixed grade, set
  <verbatim|m=degree+4>, <verbatim|D=L^d columns(stage j)>,
  <verbatim|q=exp(support+2) cameras(d)>. The five bounds reduce respectively
  to <verbatim|x\<geq\>columns(stage i)>, <verbatim|x+b\<geq\>2
  orbitCost(title+2 columns)>, <verbatim|4q\<leq\>x^3>,
  <verbatim|x+b\<geq\>1>, and <verbatim|D2^m\<leq\>x+b\<leq\>2x>; all are
  eventual lower bounds on the same variable. The fit <verbatim|minSide
  d\<leq\>radiusB(x)> follows from E01 divergence.>>|<row|<cell|One threshold
  uniform over adjacent stages and finite grade
  range>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Bandage.hiss>;
  <verbatim|YM.Push.PriceCompiler.StepStages>,
  <verbatim|.eventually_transitions>, <verbatim|.collect_upper>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Kettle.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Push/PRICE_COMPILER/Basic.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|hiss>,
  the table cost, and the scale-selection wrapper are in the actual
  <verbatim|Bandage> namespace in <verbatim|Kettle.lean>, not
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof>. For fixed <verbatim|j,i>, the grade range
  <verbatim|d\<leq\>i> is finite, so finitely many radial thresholds have a
  maximum. A fixed <verbatim|j> has only two possible stages, <verbatim|i=j>
  and <verbatim|i=j-1>. <verbatim|eventually_transitions> intersects those
  two tails. <verbatim|collect_upper> replaces these stagewise thresholds and
  the old delay entry by their finite prefix maxima, giving monotone entries;
  later delays preserve the implication. The proof in this manuscript expands
  the prefix-maximum argument.>>|<row|<cell|Actual Geyser
  consumer>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Bandage.nectar>;
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Geyser.pond>; <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Gist.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Fields/Pond.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|nectar>
  consumes <verbatim|Steam> for escape/resides and Brine, then pairs it with
  selected Minty, exponents, nest, climbing doors, and Freight; its
  <verbatim|resides> branch projects the creek inequalities into gradewise
  <verbatim|Fiesta>, <verbatim|Cherry>, <verbatim|Banks>, stencil fit, and
  place bounds. <verbatim|Geyser.pond> carries those fields into the public
  Ponds consumer. Our chapter proves the Steam numerical estimates, while the
  parent public-service chapter records the caller and downstream
  use.>>|<row|<cell|Creek inequalities project to exact Geyser service
  fields>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.PhysicalNext.Repeat.Legato.Bandage.stamina>,
  <verbatim|.evaporates>, <verbatim|.resides>;
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Fiesta>, <verbatim|Cherry>, <verbatim|Banks>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/MergeProof/Stove.lean>, <verbatim|Crisp.lean>,
  <verbatim|SpringT.lean>>|<cell|<verbatim|stamina> applies
  <verbatim|Bandage.hiss> at period <verbatim|J(m+1)> and stage
  <verbatim|J(m)> using the clock recurrence. <verbatim|resides> reindexes
  the five creek inequalities into the local room/price bounds and terminal
  support cost; it uses <verbatim|Doors.temp_cheap> to compare the positive
  finite camera threshold inverse with <verbatim|x_m>. <verbatim|evaporates>
  sets <verbatim|\<delta\>_m=probe(x_{m+1})=x_{m+1}^{-2}> and
  <verbatim|\<varphi\>_m=sap(x_{m+1})=x_{m+1}^{-1}>; the cubic mint
  inequality yields <verbatim|\<delta\>_m \<varphi\>_m mintK(B_m)\<geq\>1>,
  while <verbatim|Stock.consumes> supplies the schedule's two-step cover
  growth and <verbatim|L_m\<geq\>2> gives the split.>>|<row|<cell|Root
  scaling after moment denominator>|<cell|<verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Accent.tentF>;
  <verbatim|YM.MergeProof.Stock.spacer>, <verbatim|.tallies>;
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/FullVolume/Dusk/Tackle.lean>,
  <verbatim|Lean/YM/Overlay/Terminal.lean>>|<cell|If <verbatim|M> is the
  number of terminal-scale replicated labels and <verbatim|q=(a_m/a_k)^4>,
  then <verbatim|\|Lambda_k\|=Mq>; the coefficient price exponent
  <verbatim|\|Lambda_k\| treasury_k+6M> becomes <verbatim|M(q treasury_k+6)>
  before taking the normalized root. The root-unit argument is cited in the
  service chapter as <verbatim|ex-centered-sail>. No claim is made that the
  vacuum denominator cancels the treasury.>>>>>

  <section|Unresolved boundary><label|unresolved-boundary>

  The fixed schedule, levels, title costs, cameras, and selected run are
  inherited data in the actual producer. The same-history service chapter
  states the additional charged history and paid-response receipts
  explicitly. This unit does not prove their purchase or the nonlinear menu
  theorem supplying the selected local response.

  <section|Checks><label|checks>

  <\itemize-minus>
    <item>Read only the selected scale estimate declarations and their
    immediate dependencies listed above; made no Lean edits and ran no Lean
    build.

    <item>No external literature source is needed: the estimates are
    elementary real-variable comparisons and finite-prefix maxima, with the
    project-specific reserves identified to their pinned declarations.

    <item>Ran <verbatim|latexmk -pdf -interaction=nonstopmode -halt-on-error
    -outdir=/tmp/ym-centered-fragment-build /tmp/ym-centered-fragment.tex>;
    the temporary combined fragment compiled to 42 pages after adding this
    section. Eleven unresolved cross-references come from omitted OPE and
    lattice/column units; there were no LaTeX errors in this chapter.

    <item>Ran <verbatim|python3 scripts/check_blueprint.py>; it stopped
    because the shared parent-owned <verbatim|blueprint/units/YM-000026/unit.json>
    is absent from the clone. Do not create that shared record from this
    subtask.
  </itemize-minus>

